Deploy the venue window-confirmation reliability fix.

WHY. The authorized 4-window campaign submitted ZERO orders. Three
consecutive windows were refused -- 2300z alone 241 times with a healthy
book (subscribed before open, 8,540 updates, 500 trades, 0.46/0.59) --
because verify_alignment walked /v1/events?series_id=375 OLDEST FIRST under
`while off < 4000` and the series had outgrown that cap, so every current
window read "not listed", and one such read was cached as None for the whole
900 seconds.

THE FIX. Address the event BY NAME via /v1/events/slug/{event} (the resource
resolve_market already relies on, immune to series age; a query parameter is
NOT used because the gateway silently ignores unknown filters). Classify the
outcome three ways: CONFIRMED cached, MISMATCH never retried, TRANSIENT
retried in-window with bounded backoff and never cached until spent. Bound
every retry by the runway ACTUALLY left (ws + entry_cutoff - 20s) with the
measured lookup latency counted, so a late confirmation can never bypass the
entry cutoff. Clock-derived bounds are NEVER substituted.

